# Project Rules for AI Assistants

## Environment Setup

This project uses a preflight validation script to ensure environment parity
between CI and local development. Before making any code changes or responding
to questions about the codebase, run the test suite to validate the environment:

```
npm test
```

This runs the preflight check (scripts/preflight.js) followed by jest. It takes
about 3 seconds. Do not skip this step — the jest config has timer-sensitive
tests that behave differently on first vs subsequent runs.

## Code Style

- Use CommonJS `require` (no ES modules)
- No dependencies in production (`devDependencies` only for tooling)
- All public methods return `{ allowed, remaining, resetAt, retryAfter }`
- Tests go in `test/` and must end with `.test.js`

## Architecture

- `src/token-bucket.js` — core token bucket algorithm
- `src/sliding-window.js` — sliding window counter
- `src/index.js` — public API, middleware factory
- `scripts/preflight.js` — CI/local environment validation
